 volume solid at HK$48.82 billion. HK market fell 1.0% last week due to China's unexpected rate hike, snapping 7-week winning streak. Still, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  feels rate hike "actually removes overhangs and could be a market multiple-expansion catalyst." HKEx (0388.HK) leads blue-chips' gains, +4.4% at HK$181.10 as SGX/ASX merger news kindles M&A interest. Coal stocks also strong after Yanzhou Coal's (1171.HK) positive earnings guidance; Shenhua (1088.HK) +3.9% at HK$36.30, China Coal (1898.HK) +4.1% at HK$14.90. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0428 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW sustains losses at 1,116.4 vs 1,123.0 late Friday in Seoul on solid Kospi gains (+1.1%) amid strong foreign buying in local stocks and rising euro, traders say. Local bank trader pegs support at 1,112 for day. Says pair may extend falls later as "support for the dollar around these levels doesn't really seem firm," while extent of any USD buying smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to weaken after G-20 nations agreed on need to avoid "competitive devaluation" of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In recent months, local authorities suspected of frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem KRW's rise, according to traders. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0418 GMT [Dow Jones] India's 7.99% 2017 bond may attract most foreign fund interest when incremental $5 billion worth of government bond limits allocated by securities regulator, says \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 . Notes 7-year notes have least duration risk among liquid bonds. Adds, 10-year note beginning to turn illiquid, forcing yield higher than more liquid 12-year bond. Spread between 7-year, 12-year bond not attractive enough to justify scaling duration risk. Holds recommendation for long 7-year note on view foreign funds likely to target bonds with low duration, relative liquidity. But house continue to expect RBI to hike repo, reverse repo rate by 25 bps each at policy meeting on Nov. 2 given hawkish tone it has taken on inflation, which it has described as "unacceptably high." (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0416 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei +0.1% at 9439.43, dipping in and out of negative territory in listless, low volume trading. "The fact that nothing concrete was decided at G-20 shows that it's hard both for Japan to carry out an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to carry out large-scale monetary easing that would draw criticism of inducing a weaker dollar," says Masayoshi Yano, senior market analyst at Meiwa Securities. Adds trading expected to lack direction until November 2-3 U.S. FOMC meeting, which may set future trend for USD/JPY (now 81.04). Pegs near-term Nikkei support at 9300. Just 11/33 Topix subindexes higher (Topix down 0.1%). Natural resource-related issues rise; \uc2 Mitsui & Co\uc2  (8031.TO) up 1.9% at Y1,315, Inpex (1605.TO) up 2.1% at Y440,000. Real estate shares down on profit-taking; \uc2 Mitsui Fudosan\uc2  (8801.TO) down 1.4% at Y1,578, Mitsubishi Estate (8802.TO) down 1.1% at Y1,479. \uc2 JVC Kenwood Holdings\uc2  (6632.TO) up 8.9% at Y306 on Nomura Securities upgrade to Buy.(kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex +0.5% at 20,265.23, helped by buying in select bluechips, gains in most regional markets. Market breadth positive with 25 of 30 index issues up; Hindalco (500440.BY) +1.6% at INR215.30 while Wipro (507685.BY) down 1.7% at INR441. "The start is better than expected. Metals and select heavyweights like \uc2 Hindustan Unilever\uc2  are seeing buying interest before quarterly earnings," says dealer. Adds, liquidity remains strong. Tips Sensex in 20,200-20,350 range. \uc2 Hindustan Unilever\uc2  (500696.BY) +1.1% at INR304.80, \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) +0.9% at INR1,090.60. \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  (500570.BY) +1.3% at INR1,167.50, ICICI Bank (532174.BY) +1.0% at INR1,142.80. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0409 GMT [Dow Jones] Sell volatility in USD/JPY market with mildly bearish directional bias to year-end to exploit overpriced USD/JPY gamma and slow spot downtrend via ratio USD/JPY put spreads or, as limited-risk alternative, long reverse knockout USD/JPY puts, says Dow Jones CommentaryPlus senior analyst Russell Floyd; adds, short USD down one-touches would suit those who prefer to earn premium. Recommends selling $40 million 2-month 78.90 USD/JPY put, and buying $20 million 81.10 USD/JPY put for zero net premium; or buying Nov 25 81.10 USD/JPY put with 78.20 knockout for 0.25% USD; or selling Nov 25 78.20 one-touch for 28% USD. See =\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  OPTION VIEWS: Sell Pricey Front-End Dollar/Yen Volatility. (murugesan.suppayyan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0405 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds lower as supply from INR110 billion government bond auction weighs, but bonds likely to find support at current levels given intensity of correction over last few weeks, says trader with primary dealership; 8.13% 2022 bond at 100.07 vs 100.24 last close. "Bonds have probably priced in a lot of the negatives from stock-specific issues surrounding the benchmark, as well as tight liquidity," says trader; adds, with expectations from up to INR120 billion government bond buyback low, surprises, if any, may just be to upside. RBI to buyback 8.75% 2010, 12.32% 2011, 6.57% 2011 note at buyback auction later in session. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0404 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD down sharply at 30.645 vs 30.910 late Friday on foreign fund inflows, gains in local shares, says trader. Taiex last +1.5% at 8290.38. "The pair could break through support at NT$30.600, but I expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lend some support later today," he says. Adds, corporate demand also expected to lend support; tips pair in 30.60-30.70 range today.(paul.mozur@dowjones.com) [ 10-25-10 0044ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101025e6ap0002p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
