\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Strong growth, shekel create dilemma for Israel cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 911 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2010\par 13:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 2-year high, hurting exports\par \par \uc2 * House prices driving surge in inflation\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiking rates while buying dollars\par \par \uc2 * Analysts see unorthodox twin-track policy continuing\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Concerns about price pressures at home and a shaky economic outlook abroad mean the Bank of Israel looks set to continue raising interest rates while buying dollars as the price of keeping an export-driven recovery on track.\par \par \uc2 Inflation worries prompted mainly by the surging cost of housing together with a rampant stock market -- Tel Aviv share indices are at all-time highs -- have led to a series of rate hikes over the past year.\par \par \uc2 Those moves, along with expectations of more tightening that would further widen the rate differential between Israel and the United States, have helped propel the local shekel \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <ILS=> to a two-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 That in turn has eroded the competitiveness of the country's exports, which account for more than 40 percent of economic activity, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought tens of billions of dollars to try to slow the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 At a time of marked dollar weakness, Israel's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are rising steadily and topped $66 billion in September, more than double the level of two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Central banks typically do not raise rates -- putting upward pressure on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the same time.\par \par \uc2 But many analysts believe Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer has little choice but to carry on doing just that.\par \par \uc2 "By stopping \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  he would infuriate exporters and if he stopped raising rates, it could create a housing bubble and risk higher inflation especially with (global) oil prices going up," said Elisabeth Gruie, a strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BITING THE BULLET\par \par \uc2 Rafi Gozlan, an economist at Leader Capital Markets, said Fischer will continue to do both for as long as it takes to help the Israeli economy, which could face slower growth in 2011 due weakness abroad, notably in the United States and Europe.\par \par \uc2 In a possible foretaste, the statistics bureau trimmed its 2010 growth estimate on Sunday to 4 pct of GDP from 4.1 pct, saying it now expected exports to expand by 9.1 pct rather than the 13.1 percent it forecast just a month ago. [ID:nLDE69G069]\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in March 2008 with purchases of $25 million a day. Now it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it deems necessary and has bought more than $1 billion in the past month.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the main reason that enabled Israeli exports to survive," said Ori Yehudai, chairman of the economics committee at Israel's manufacturers' Association. "We are competing in a very competitive world."\par \par \uc2 But the Finance Ministry has criticised both the rate hikes and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying the rates gap with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  was leading to speculation and that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was losing money by holding such high foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Israel is not a bank of profits," Fischer said on Oct. 3 in response, while holding out against government proposals to tax speculators.\par \par \uc2 BALANCING ACT\par \par \uc2 Israel, a high-tech powerhouse, experienced only a minor hit from the global crisis. The economy is forecast to grow at least 4 percent this year and at a slightly slower pace in 2011, well above estimates for the United States and Europe.\par \par \uc2 Annual inflation, at 1.8 percent in August, is meanwhile expected to reach 3 percent in the coming year -- the top end of a target of 1-3 percent. House prices in particular have jumped.\par \par \uc2 "(Fischer) needs to perform a balancing act," said \uc2 UBS\uc2  economist Reinhard Cluse. "He needs to ensure against all kinds of risks like a global double dip (recession), which would hit the Israeli economy. On the other hand there is a risk to inflation, with the real estate market turning into a bubble."\par \par \uc2 Since August 2009, Israel has raised its benchmark rate by 1.5 percentage points to 2 percent and most analysts see one more hike by year-end, with the rate above 3 percent in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Cluse views Fischer's rate hikes as measured to limit further shekel gains while avoiding stifling economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "At 2 percent, rates are above the United States and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but still... quite accommodative," he said.\par \par \uc2 The shekel stands at around 3.58 per dollar, rising nearly 7 percent since rate hikes resumed in late July. Fischer contends the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has also been bolstered by a current account surplus, would be stronger still but for the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts remain bullish on the shekel, given expectations of further easing measures by the U.S. Federal Reserve and scope for more Israel rate hikes. \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  on Thursday forecast a rate of 3.30 per dollar within six months.\par \par \uc2 "If you have a strong economy, you have a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," added Psagot brokerage chief economist Vered Dar, who questions the wisdom of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's approach.\par \par \uc2 "The interest rate tool isn't sharp enough to help with housing prices," she said, noting it took 400 basis points of hikes over two years last decade to cool the U.S. property market.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Tova Cohen; Editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-CENTRALBANK/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|MD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101021e6ai0011k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
