\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 6-World finance leaders seek to avoid  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  clash\b0\par\par\uc2 984 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2010\par 17:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Finance chiefs seek sounder recovery, no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war\par \par \uc2 * China says moving on yuan but at its own pace\par \par \uc2 * IMF being tailored for heightened management role (Adds Canadian finance minister, details on IMF plan)\par \par \uc2 By Jan Strupczewski and Gernot Heller\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Global finance chiefs sought on Friday to prevent tensions over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  valuations from derailing a fragile economic recovery, and stressed they must work together to find ways to rebalance global growth.\par \par \uc2 Ministers from the Group of 20 nations repeated a call for export powerhouses, such as China, to spend more at home so indebted countries, like the United States, can rebuild their finances without risking a still-fragile global recovery.\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund, heading into evening talks with the Group of Seven rich countries, was seeking support for a more active role in monitoring the world's major economies.\par \par \uc2 Officials worry that a weak U.S. dollar and relatively strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  elsewhere could push nations into a round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciations to help their exports.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a 15-year low against the yen on Friday after a U.S. report of more job losses cemented expectations of a further loosening in an already-easy U.S. monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The uneven pattern of global growth has seen U.S. interest rates cut to nearly zero, driving capital into emerging markets and prompting talk of a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war." At the same time, China has allowed its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise only slowly.\par \par \uc2 "I'm not in the mind or in the mood for war, this is totally inadequate, inappropriate and unnecessary," French Finance Minister Christine Lagarde said.\par \par \uc2 The United States urged the IMF to act as a more forceful global overseer. Finance chiefs were working toward giving the Fund a redefined role, possibly by the time G20 political leaders meet in Korea in November.\par \par \uc2 The IMF's managing director, Dominique Strauss-Kahn, sought support for a "systemic stability initiative" to keep a closer watch on the largest economies and ensure they do not put the world in danger of financial crisis again.\par \par \uc2 He seemed to be winning some allies. Svein Gjedrem, a Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, speaking on behalf of Nordic and Baltic countries, said he supported developing an IMF-coordinated framework.\par \par \uc2 "In the post-crisis period, IMF surveillance will be of growing importance and acquire a greater role in preventing crises, both in individual countries and global," he said.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner called on the IMF to "speak out effectively about challenges and marshal support for action."\par \par \uc2 Taking a jab at China, Geithner complained that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by countries trying to keep undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating threatened the global recovery.\par \par \uc2 China pushed back by saying it will move ahead with exchange-rate reforms at its own pace.\par \par \uc2 "We still think China needs a market-based exchange rate regime," China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Zhou Xiaochuan, said. "I think the difference is that for China, we view it as gradualism, a gradual way, rather than shock therapy."\par \par \uc2 Canadian Finance Minister Jim Flaherty said he expected advanced economies to put up a united front in prodding China and other countries to allow more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, but said no broad \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accord would be reached.\par \par \uc2 "I certainly don't anticipate there's going to be any unanimous agreement here in Washington on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 The chairman of the euro zone finance ministers, Jean-Claude Juncker, said part of the problem was a lack of a suitable forum for bringing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  negotiations to a point.\par \par \uc2 "In the G20 framework there are too many people and too many interests to be able to find a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  arrangement," he told Reuters. "The ideal forum would be G7 plus China."\par \par \uc2 The G7 is comprised of the Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japan last month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in six years to stem a rise in the yen. Many emerging economies have taken steps to try to slow a rising tide of inflows of foreign capital.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL APPROACH\par \par \uc2 Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega, who earlier this week doubled a tax on foreign funds flooding into his country's bond markets, called for a sweeping new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deal.\par \par \uc2 "I think in the G20 meetings we can arrive at an agreement something like the Plaza Accord," he said, referring to a 1985 agreement among the world's then trade powers to push down the dollar's value.\par \par \uc2 Other officials said countries should let market forces determine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values.\par \par \uc2 G20 nations have committed to a process in which the IMF helps them coordinate on policies to rebalance global growth, but cooperation has frayed because of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions.\par \par \uc2 Zhou said China was pursuing policies to boost demand at home, including improvements to its social security system, allowing Chinese consumers to save less and spend more.\par \par \uc2 The yuan hit its highest closing level on Friday since a landmark revaluation in July 2005, possibly a sign Beijing is sensitive to the demands its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should rise faster.\par \par \uc2 Donald Straszheim, senior managing director for China research at ISI Group in Los Angeles, was skeptical that the G20 would make much ground in pushing China on the yuan.\par \par \uc2 "Zhou said again this morning essentially: 'our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , our business, our pace'," he said.\par \par \uc2 Expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve will further ease monetary policy -- bolstered by Friday's report showing the U.S. economy unexpectedly lost 95,000 jobs last month -- has pushed the dollar to an 8-1/2-month low against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Additional reporting by Reuters IMF team; writing by Emily Kaiser and Glenn Somerville; editing by Tim Ahmann and Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 IMF/ (WRAPUP 6) (PIX)|LANGEN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|ABX|BNX|SXNA    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101008e6a8001nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
