\par\par \b \uc2 FXOUTLOOK-US dollar likely to remain under pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2010\par 17:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Dollar likely to fall in coming week, technicals weak\par \par \uc2 * Fears of U.S. quantitative easing hurt the dollar\par \par \uc2 * Investors remain on alert for Bank of Japan activity\par \par \uc2 By Nick Olivari\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The dollar is likely to fall in the week ahead after breaching several technical support levels on expectations of more monetary easing by the Federal Reserve.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it stood ready to provide additional support to bolster the economic recovery. The euro and yen immediately gained on the news. The euro had its best week since late May, 2009 and the yen the best week since mid July, 2010.\par \par \uc2 Any further stimulus, particularly U.S. Treasury debt purchases, will push benchmark yields lower and further diminish the return on dollar-denominated assets.\par \par \uc2 The dollar is also under pressure against the yen. However, fears the Bank of Japan will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will limit the greenback's downside.\par \par \uc2 "The best we can hope for is to cap the dollar's downtrend," said Omer Esiner, chief market analyst at \uc2 Commonwealth \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Inc\uc2  in Washington. "Soft U.S. data will only fan concerns about the Fed's quantitative easing."\par \par \uc2 But "softer-than-expected bond auctions (in Europe) or Irish bank headlines will cap the euro gains," said Esiner.\par \par \uc2 Concerns that some Irish banks could default on their debt causing wider problems in the euro zone had weighed on the euro in recent weeks though that was not apparent in the last few days. The euro rose 3.3 percent this week against the dollar as the dollar fell 1.7 percent against the yen.\par \par \uc2 Moments after the Fed announcement, the euro/dollar broke above the 200-day simple moving average and kept going. Long-term moving averages are strong resistance levels or once breached become long-term support.\par \par \uc2 "The trend on euro/dollar continues for the time being to be to the upside, and steeply so," said \uc2 James Chen\uc2 , chief technical strategist, at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Solutions\uc2 . "If the trend is to continue this steep ascent, a strong breakout above $1.3400 should confirm the pair's bullishness, with an upside target around $1.3800."\par \par \uc2 Chen places strong downside support at the $1.3000 psychological level. The euro was last at $1.3475.\par \par \uc2 YEN PRESSURE\par \par \uc2 The dollar is likely to remain pressured against the yen on the same concerns about quantitative easing. At the same time, investors are on full alert for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 The yen rose as high as 85.94 yen on electronic trading platform EBS the day after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 15. It has since eased back. The spot rate was last at 84.26 yen on Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Investors had bet that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hold the 85 level but that came and went without any action from the bank.\par \par \uc2 A sudden slide in the yen against the dollar Friday during Tokyo trading stirred suspicions of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But by the time New York opened for business, traders had mostly discounted official action.\par \par \uc2 The yen move followed a meeting between Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan and U.S. President Barack Obama in New York Thursday where \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not even discussed, a sign to some the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  was taking a hands off approach.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's recent declines against the yen have now breached the 50 percent Fibonacci retracement of the rapid move from the low of 82.87 before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the peak at 85.94 after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on electric trading platform EBS.\par \par \uc2 Chen of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Solutions\uc2  said dollar/yen price action placed it squarely in the confines of a continuing downtrend extending back to the May high around 95 yen. Chen places technical support at 83 and resistance at 86.\par \par \uc2 On the sidelines, investors are watching for potential U.S. import duties on goods from countries that undervalue their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a U.S. congressional panel approved a bill Friday..\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers have long threatened legislation if China did not take action to increase the value of the yuan, and unlike the Obama-Kan talks, exchange rates were a key element of talks between Obama and Chinese premier Wen Jiabao this week.\par \par \uc2 But "it will not have too much impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," said John Doyle, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Tempus Consulting in Washington. "It's more rhetorical" (Reporting by Nick Olivari; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /OUTLOOK|LANGEN|FUN    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100924e69o001fj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
