\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY MARKETS-Three-month euro Libor nears lifetime low\b0\par\par\uc2 By George Matlock   \par \uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2009\par 16:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 12 (Reuters) - Three-month euro funding costs inched close to lifetime lows on Thursday and sterling hit another lowest level since 1986, but the cost of dollar funds edged up at the British Bankers' Association London fixings.\par \par \uc2 Three-month London interbank offered rates over OIS rates for dollars steadied at 97 basis points. But the spread and three-month Libor rates remained wide enough to reveal market disappointment with a lack of detail in U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner's bank-rescue plan and broader concerns about banking sector losses.\par \par \uc2 The euro Libor rate fixing <EUR3MFSR=> was at 1.95625 percent, just shy of 1.95525 percent hit in March 2004 -- the lowest point since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's creation in 1989, according to Reuters charts. Back in 2004 the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key interest rate was at 2.0 percent, as it is now.\par \par \uc2 The decline in the three-month euro Libor rate came after the key three-month Euribor bank-to-bank euro lending rate fell below the ECB's official rate on Thursday and moved within touching distance of the all-time low. [ID:nFAE002843]\par \par \uc2 The three-month Euribor rate <EURIBOR3MD=>, traditionally the main gauge of the interbank euro lending and a mix of interest rate expectations and banks' appetite for lending, fell to 1.959 percent from 1.975 percent.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters data, the all-time low is 1.957 percent, set in March 2004.\par \par \uc2 "The 3-month euro Libor hit 1.95625 percent, so the smooth downward trend of around 1.5 basis points per day is still firmly in place also in the month of February," said David Schnautz, market analyst at Commzerzbank in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 "Overnight Libor in euro funds is still volatile so far this month, hovering between 1.13 percent and 1.228 percent but obviously declining to the lower end of that range now," he added.\par \par \uc2 Banks' overnight borrowing from the ECB rose to a three-month high but deposits eased, figures showed on Thursday resulting in lower euro Libor rates.\par \par \uc2 The ECB said banks borrowed 10.405 billion euros from its overnight loan facility, up from the 3.697 billion taken previously and the highest amount borrowed since Nov. 10.\par \par \uc2 Banks deposited 97.760 billion euros overnight as of Feb. 11, down from the 103.545 billion euros reported on Wednesday, but still showing that many institutions prefer to park excess cash at the ECB than lend it on to peers.\par \par \uc2 "It may look as though banks are recycling money a little bit more than usual, being well down from the 180 billion euros deposits seen before," said David Keeble, global head of interest rate strategy at Calyon in London. "However, we are at the start of the reserve period and so they seem to be taking less cash in the weekly repos."\par \par \uc2 The ECB introduced changes in January which it hoped would make depositing cash at the ECB less attractive and encourage banks back into interbank lending.\par \par \uc2 EURO FOLLOWS STERLING\par \par \uc2 The three-month sterling Libor rate <GBP3MFSR=> reached 2.07 percent, its lowest since 1986, according to Reuters charts.\par \par \uc2 This compared with 6.80 percent in early September as the credit crisis came to a head and resulted in the collapse of investment bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Conversely, three-month dollar Libor rates <USD3MFSR=>, which had declined since October and reached 1.08250 percent on Jan. 14, was fixed at 1.23438 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve cut its key policy rate to a zero to 0.25 percent range in December and efforts to stimulate the world's biggest economy have shifted to other instruments including fiscal measures such as U.S. President Barack Obama's economic stimulus package. [ID:nN12436678].\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of England and ECB are still in rate-cut mode, dove-tailed by various \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whereas in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  hope for a kind of quick-fix have been disappointed by Geithner which holds off three-month Libor from approaching its lows again," said Schnautz.\par \par \uc2 However, three-month dollar Libor had risen only slightly from Wednesday's fixing and seemed to be stabilising between 1.20 percent and 1.25 percent since the start of the month.\par \par \uc2 MONEYMARKETS/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|NAT|UKI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090212e52c002lt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
