\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Dollar heading in right direction - Juncker\b0\par\par\uc2 By Darren Ennis   \par \uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2008\par 19:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS , Sept 1 (Reuters) - The head of the eurogroup of countries that share the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday welcomed the recent recovery of the U.S. dollar, but said the euro remained overvalued.\par \par \uc2 "Things are developing in the right direction," Jean-Claude Juncker told Reuters after an EU leaders summit in Brussels. Juncker is prime minister of Luxembourg.\par \par \uc2 "Things are more in line with the economic policy and commitments of the United States that have been stated in recent months," he said.\par \par \uc2 Eurozone officials expressed frustration earlier this year that, despite comments by top U.S. policy-makers in support of a strong dollar, the greenback remained in the doldrums.\par \par \uc2 "A strong dollar is good for the United States. A strong dollar is good for the global economy," Juncker said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the euro was closer to fair value now against the dollar, Juncker said: "In line with what we have previously said, we still think that the euro is still overvalued."\par \par \uc2 The dollar, which sank to a low of more than $1.60 to the euro in July, was trading at around $1.47 at 1830 GMT on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar rose to its highest level this year during the day, boosted by a sharp drop in oil prices. U.S. crude oil futures <CLc1> fell $4.51 to $110.95 a barrel in afternoon trading on Monday after Hurricane Gustav weakened to a Category 2 storm before hitting the coast near a key port that supports most of the Gulf of Mexico oil and gas drilling \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Europe, and Japan had discussed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rescue the dollar if it extended the sharp losses it was suffering at the time, an international finance source told Reuters last week.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced renewed criticism earlier this year from some European leaders, including French President Nicolas Sarkozy, alarmed at the strength of the euro that has made it harder for European exporters to compete. (Reporting by Darren Ennis; Editing by William Schomberg and Jan Paschal)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -EURO/JUNCKER (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|BNX|ABX|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|UKI|J|Z|SI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080901e491001w0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
