\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-US dlr fall risk to world economy - Indonesia cbanker.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Stella Dawson  \par \uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2005\par 23:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BASEL, Switzerland, Jan 9 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar has depreciated over the past year by more than the world's top central bankers had expected and currently poses one of the greatest challenges to the global economy, a senior Indonesian monetary official said on Sunday.  \par \par \uc2 But Miranda Goeltom, senior deputy governor of Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in an interview with Reuters that G3 nations should wait for the U.S. government to tackle its budget and trade deficits before considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem dollar weakness.  \par \par \uc2 "The magnitude of the depreciation is more than one would have expected," Goeltom told Reuters on the sidelines of the G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings in Basel on the global economy.  \par \par \uc2 Increasingly, central bankers worry that the massive U.S. budget and trade deficits will trigger a dollar rout that could destabilise financial markets worldwide.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar  has shed more than 25 percent of its value against a basket\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since early 2003, with losses accelerating since\par President George W. Bush won re-election in November. The euro hit a\par record high last month above 1.36        and the Japanese yen a 4-year\par high at 102       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While dollar depreciation against the yen and euro was expected in 2004 and movements have not been excessively volatile, Goeltom said the size had been the surprise.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The fact that there are still big questions as to where the dollar goes, the yen goes, the euro goes, has made it more difficult, of course, to account for exchange rate risk in the calculations of business people," she said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asked whether the United States, Japan and Europe, known as the G3, should consider buying dollars in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stem its decline or should leave its course to be corrected by changes in macro-economic policies, Goeltom said there were numerous opinions on the matter.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think both can be done, with the major role (being) the improvement of the real source of the problem. For example, I would think it would be better that rates should be higher and the effort of the U.S. government to address the problems of the budget and trade deficits, rather than the (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) rate should be borne by G3 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," she said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A widening U.S. current account deficit to more than 5 percent of GDP and growing is the root cause of dollar weakness, as investors grow reluctant to lend the United States ever more money to finance its appetite for imports and for government spending.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial markets are waiting for the Bush administration early next month to unveil a credible program to reduce the yawning U.S. budget deficit. Indeed U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow on Friday gave the dollar a lift by promising to "do things" and work with Congress to reduce the deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There will be a market mechanism" in response to U.S. action on its budget deficit, Goeltom said.Some financial analysts predict the G3 will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United States\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  starts to turn the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around with a deficit reduction program.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUPIAH TOO CHEAP  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the Indonesian rupiah , Goeltom said that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  watches the inflationary dangers created by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation and is ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if needed. But any rupiah purchases would not be targeted at a specific exchange rate level, only on inflationary impact.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost more than 6 percent in value the past year, due to costlier imported crude oil and the economic expansion which has created demanded for foreign capital goods. Additionally, recent elections caused investor reluctance to invest in Indonesia until the political environment settled, creating pressures on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goeltom said that the rupiah at 9,280 - its closing price on Friday - was undervalued. Asked whether 9,000 would be a more appropriate value, she said: "I would think so."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 She said she expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate to that level by the end of 2005 on the back of inward investment, which she sees rising by 20 percent this year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050109e11900hz9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
