\par\par \b \uc2 SCHEDULE-Reuters Business Report at 1330 GMT.   \b0\par\par\uc2 1,103 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2004\par 14:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Editor: Chris Johnson   \par \par \uc2 Telephone: +44 20 7542 6658   \par \par \uc2 Following are some of the main business news stories (all times GMT) which have moved or are expected to move in the next few hours.   \par \par \uc2 TOP HEADLINES   \par \par \uc2 LONDON-Oil price falls to 3-month low   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG/SAN FRANCISCO-China's Lenovo buys IBM PC unit   \par \par \uc2 LONDON-Oil companies lead stocks lower   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT-Revamped sports car icon Porsche boosts sales   \par \par \uc2 LONDON - Mild winter weather in United States and expectations of rise in heating fuel stocks push oil prices to three-month lows (MARKETS-OIL (UPDATE 3), moved at 1222, 420 words)   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG/SAN FRANCISCO - IBM is selling PC-making business to China's largest personal computer company, Lenovo Group, for $1.25 billion, marking U.S. firm's retreat from industry it helped pioneer (TECH-CHINA-IBM-SALE (UPDATE 5), moved at 1043, picture, by Tony Munroe and Eric Auchard, 860 words)   \par \par \uc2 LONDON - European stocks follow Wall Street lower as crude oil's slide to three-month lows hits heavily weighted oil shares, although a recovering dollar was a plus for region's exporters (MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 3), moved at 1150, by William Kemble-Diaz, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT - Porsche boosts car sales 7 percent in four months to Nov. 30, 2004 over a year ago, mainly on strong demand for its 911 sports car and Cayenne offroader as rejuvenated line-up ensures growth (AUTOS-PORSCHE (UPDATE 2), moved at 1122, by Christiaan Hetzner, 570 words)   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 COMPANIES:   \par \par \uc2 HELSINKI/LONDON - Finland sells up to 6.4 percent of Nordic telecoms operator TeliaSonera as the firm writes off book value of its International Carrier unit to zero, sending shares lower (TELECOMS-TELIASONERA (UPDATE 2), moved at 1152, by Ott Ummelas and Alison Tudor, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Russia hits No. 2 telecoms firm VimpelCom with $158 million back tax claim for 2001, sending shockwaves across markets fearing Kremlin wants bigger slice of economy (TELECOMS-RUSSIA-VIMPELCOM (UPDATE 2), moved at 1234, by Maxim Filimonov, 710 words)   \par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS - Microsoft may deploy strategy that neatly sidesteps objections by European regulators in push to control anti-piracy software, experts say (TECH-CONTENTGUARD-EU (ANALYSIS), moved at 1109, by David Lawsky, 660 words)   \par \par \uc2 MILAN - Shares in Telecom Italia and TIM touch highest levels in nearly three years a day after telecoms group announces 21-billion-euro buyout of its mobile unit (TELECOMS-TIM-T.ITALIA (UPDATE 4), expect by 1600, by William Schomberg and Clara Ferreira-Marques, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 LONDON - Standard Chartered says consumer banking revenues will be flat in Hong Kong, its biggest market, sending shares lower despite in-line forecast for overall 2004 profit (FINANCIAL-STANCHART (UPDATE 3), moved at 1227, by Sean Farrell, 610 words)   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS:   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK - U.S. stocks look to open flat, one day after sharp sell-off, as oil prices slip lower while a major sale is announced by IBM (MARKETS-USA-STOCKS (UPDATE 3), expect by 1440, 300 words)   \par \par \uc2 LONDON - Dollar gains ground as investors take profits from other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on signs \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength may prompt some central banks to scale back interest rate tightening (MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 5), moved at 1315, by Katie Hunt, 700 words)   \par \par \uc2 LONDON - Euro will probably set fresh highs against dollar in next month, before stronger data from \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and possibly, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bring rally to an end, Reuters poll suggests; Reuters has surveyed more than 50 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists on outlook for dollar exchange rates against euro, yen, sterling and Swiss franc (MARKETS-POLL-EURO, moved at 1231, by Toni Vorobyova, 750 words)   \par \par \uc2 See also   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-POLL-POUND, moved at 1133, by Natalie Harrison, 600 words   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-POLL-SWISS, moved at 1239, by Natalie Harrison, 500 words   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-POLL-VOLATILITY, moving shortly, 300 words   \par \par \uc2 LONDON - Gold and benchmark industrial metal copper fall sharply from recent multi-year peaks, as funds jittery about economic growth take dollar rebound as chance to jettison holdings (MARKETS-METALS (UPDATE 1), moved at 1249, by Veronica Brown, 550 words)   \par \par \uc2 CAIRO - Nervous OPEC oil producers size up how fast this week's ministerial meeting should rein in a supply surge that has helped cut crude prices by a quarter in barely six weeks (ENERGY-OPEC (UPDATE 3), moving shortly, by Edmund Blair and Barbara Lewis, 620 words)   \par \par \uc2 LONDON - Bank of England's laissez-faire approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates is making sterling an attractive bet for dollar bears who have sights set on psychological $2 mark (MARKETS-STERLING-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 , expect by 1500, by Christina Fincher, 710 words)   \par \par \uc2 PARIS - French grains office ONIC cuts estimate of wheat exports this season as ample supplies, weak dollar and firm freight rates take toll, and first forecast for next season shows even more wheat will be sown (FOOD-FRANCE-ONIC (UPDATE 2), expect by 1600, by Sybille de La Hamaide, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY:   \par \par \uc2 THE HAGUE - Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao says China will move gradually to flexible exchange rate but will take into account need to maintain stability of economy and those of neighbours (ECONOMY-CHINA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1), moved at 1258, 350 words)   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it is considering changing the structure of its financial reserves - the largest outside Asia and rising fast on the back of high oil prices - amid speculation it could increase its holding of euros (ECONOMY-RUSSIA-RESERVES (UPDATE 2), moving shortly, by Meg Clothier, 450 words)   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK - New applications for U.S. home mortgages increase as purchase activity rises amid lower mortgage rates, industry group says (ECONOMY-MORTGAGES (UPDATE 1), moved at 1248, 300 words)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Japan's economy barely grew in three months to September as private consumption slowed, revised government figures show, confirming widespread view that economy is weaker than thought (ECONOMY-JAPAN (UPDATE 4), moved at 0907, by Yoko Nishikawa, 800 words)   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil - Brazil's benchmark IPCA consumer price index rose 0.69 percent in November, faster than in previous month, led by jump in fuel costs (ECONOMY-BRAZIL-INFLATION (UPDATE 2), moved at 1253, by Terry Wade, 450 words)   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW/LONDON - Central Europe may be fighting a lost battle trying to restrain buoyant \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against powerful forces unleashed by weak dollar and economic dividends of European Union membership (ECONOMY-NEWCOMERS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS), expect by 1430, by Tomasz Janowski and James Thornhill, 650 words)   \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE - Czech consumer inflation backs off 2-1/2 year high in November; coupled with a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this sustains expectations in financial markets that new EU member's interest rates will stay put for many months (ECONOMY-CZECH-INFLATION (UPDATE 1), moved at 1135, by Marek Petrus, 530 words).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041208e0c80069g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
