\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slides, but climbs against Canadian dollar.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Plumberg  \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 22:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The dollar edged lower on Tuesday, although it rose against the Canadian dollar after Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled its strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would eventually affect domestic demand and prevent rate hikes.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Canada kept its overnight interest rate unchanged at 2.5 percent, citing the dampening effects of the stronger Canadian dollar. Higher rates usually attract foreign investors to invest in a particular country's assets, increasing the allure of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reaction "was off-center of the recent U.S. dollar trend," said Lara Rhame, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Credit Suisse First Boston in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had only a few weeks ago hit a 12-year low against the Canadian dollar, on a general downtrend triggered by U.S. deficit concerns.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Canada's rate decision Tuesday pushed the U.S. dollar to a one-month high against the Canadian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the news out of the Bank of Canada or the dollar/Canada price action really alters anything about the U.S. (dollar) trend," added Rhame.  \par \par \uc2 "What it does do is really put the magnifying glass on how other central banks are already substituting a tighter monetary policy for a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Analysts will focus on statements following Australian and New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings on Wednesday and Thursday respectively, to see if the U.S. dollar's weakness is affecting these countries in the same way as Canada.  \par \par \uc2 During the London trading session, the dollar slid to new lows near $1.3470 per euro as investors, tiring of tough talk from Europe on exchange rates, dismissed new warnings from euro zone finance ministers about the dangers of the rising euro.  \par \par \uc2 European finance ministers said in a joint statement after meeting in Brussels on Monday that "excessive volatility and disorderly movements" in exchange rates were hurting growth and that they would monitor the situation closely.  \par \par \uc2 These comments - the group's most stark warning to date on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates - took on added weight with the backing of European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Jean-Claude Trichet.  \par \par \uc2 But analysts said the remarks echoed what euro zone finance ministers have been saying individually for some time and were unlikely to trouble the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has shown little inclination to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the dollar's slide.  \par \par \uc2 "The finance ministers are not really going beyond statements that have already been put out, and until something new is said, we will see the dollar going lower," said Larry Brickman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America in New York.  \par \par \uc2 OH CANADA  \par \par \uc2 By 4:22 p.m. (2122 GMT) in New York, the euro had pared its gains but still was up around 0.2 percent against the dollar at $1.3428.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sterling  was up 0.35 percent at $1.9456, having earlier pushed above\par $1.95 for a new 12-year high. The dollar lost 0.1 percent against the\par Swiss franc        to 1.1402 francs.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against the yen , the dollar fell 0.3 percent to 102.87 yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was up 0.6 percent against the Canadian unit at C$1.2079, having earlier risen as high as C$1.2112.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a reversal from earlier communiques, the Bank of Canada dropped references to the need to reduce monetary stimulus further, suggesting it might slow down the pace of tightening.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the Canadian economy can adjust at 80 U.S. cents, then the Bank of Canada can start raising rates," said Jeremy Friesen, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at RBC Capital Markets in Toronto.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But if not, it will have to do something that will result in Canadian dollar weakness - either a pause in the tightening cycle or, in the extreme, reversing course," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c700ga5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
