\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits new low vs euro, jumps vs Canadian.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrea Ricci  \par \uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 19:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped to new record lows against the euro on Tuesday but rallied against the Canadian dollar after Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded to its strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by putting monetary tightening on hold.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar slid to new lows near $1.3470 per euro as investors, tiring of tough talk on exchange rates by European officials, dismissed new warnings from euro zone finance ministers about the dangers of the rising euro.  \par \par \uc2 In a joint statement, European finance ministers meeting in Brussels late on Monday charged that "excessive volatility and disorderly movements" in exchange rates were hurting growth.  \par \par \uc2 These comments, which were the group's starkest warning to date on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , took on added meaning by winning the backing of European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Jean-Claude Trichet.  \par \par \uc2 But analysts said the remarks echoed what euro zone finance ministers have been saying separately for some time and were unlikely to trouble the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has shown little inclination to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the dollar's slide.  \par \par \uc2 "The finance ministers are not really going beyond statements that have already been put out, and until something new is said, we will see the dollar going lower," said Larry Brickman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America in New York.  \par \par \uc2 By early afternoon in New York, the euro had pared its gains but still was up a quarter percent against the dollar at $1.3433 .   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sterling was up 0.39 percent at $1.9462, having earlier pushed through\par $1.95  for a new 12-year high. The dollar lost a quarter percent\par against the Swiss franc to 1.1385 francs       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell 0.45 percent to 102.73 yen .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said a report in the Wall Street Journal Europe questioning the U.S. government's triple-A bond rating also hurt the greenback.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It was one more excuse to push the dollar to new lows," said Brickman.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CANADA PAUSES  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar spiked higher against the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the Bank of Canada opted to keep its overnight rate unchanged at 2.50 percent, citing the dampening effects of the stronger Canadian dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By early afternoon, the dollar was up 0.63 percent against the Canadian unit at C$1.2073 (CAD=, having earlier risen as high as C$1.2112.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a major reversal from earlier communiques, the bank dropped references to the need to reduce monetary stimulus further, suggesting it might slow down the pace of tightening.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the Canadian economy can adjust at 80 U.S. cents, then the Bank of Canada can start raising rates," said Jeremy Freisen, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at RBC Capital Markets in Toronto.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But if not, it will have to do something that will result in Canadian dollar weakness, either a pause in the tightening cycle or, in the extreme, reversing course," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bob Lynch, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at BNP Paribas in New York, noted that the Canadian dollar has been weakening versus the U.S. dollar since late November after months of relentless gains that had taken it to 12-year highs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But going forward, the outlook for the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  largely depends on how the U.S. dollar fares generally.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the dollar continues to fall against the other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it would limit the ability of dollar/Canada to move up. But if a correction of the dollar happens more broadly, then the prospects for dollar/Canada are more bullish," Lynch said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c700c48\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
