\par\par \b \uc2 US would  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  only when euro/dlr $1.45-paper.  \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2004\par 18:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar only if the euro-dollar rate reached $1.45, a German newspaper reported on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar reached a new record low against the euro on Friday of $1.34.  \par \par \uc2 Citing a high ranking official of the U.S. Treasury Department, Germany's Boersen Zeitung said the United States at the earliest would be prepared to consider supporting the dollar if "if it fell below the 1.45 mark" to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 In an article released in advanced of publication on Saturday, the paper also said Treasury Secretary John Snow has recognised the long-term dangers of the U.S. budget and current account deficits for the economy and he accepts that exchange rate corrections are among the "most effective instruments" to slowly reduce the current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 European leaders are worried about the tumbling dollar but have not agreed to fire off their big cannon of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, senior officials of European governments said on Friday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the euro's rapid ascent should only take place in "exceptional circumstances" and now was not the right time, senior German government sources said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Another senior euro zone finance ministry official told Reuters late on Thursday that euro zone finance ministers had "absolutely not" instructed the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041203e0c300c1k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
