\par\par \b \uc2 Oil spike maybe a factor in dollar fall in May-Fed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2004\par 22:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NEW YORK, Aug 5 (Reuters) - Attacks on foreign workers in\par the Middle East and a rise in oil prices that followed may have\par been a factor in the dollar's decline at the end of May, the\par Federal Reserve Bank of New York said in a report on Thursday.\par     As expected, the Fed's quarterly report on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said U.S. monetary authorities did not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets during the April-June quarter.\par     At the end of May, attacks on foreign oil workers in Saudi\par Arabia and the subsequent rise in oil prices "may have also\par contributed to the dollar's decline" as well as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par investors' focus on the U.S. current account deficit, it said.\par     "Increased geopolitical tension was cited as a background\par factor in the dollar's inability to sustain its initial\par appreciation," by market participants, the report added.\par  \par     During the three months to the end of June, the dollar rose\par 4.4 percent against the yen and 1.0 percent against the euro.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The dollar appreciated broadly early in the period amid\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 better-than-expected U.S. economic data and increasing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expectations for U.S. monetary policy to tighten faster than  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 previously expected," the report said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But later in the quarter, the dollar reversed some of these  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gains "as concerns regarding the potential pace of monetary  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tightening in the United States moderated," the report said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen depreciated nearly 9 percent against the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from March 31 to May 14 despite stronger-than-expected Japanese  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic data and a cessation of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 to weaken the yen, the report noted.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United States\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , "Market participants remained wary of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 price pressures in the U.S. economy and their possible effect  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on the value of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as well as the potential for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reduced foreign demand for U.S. bonds and equities," it said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CONTRASTING ECB, FED RATE EXPECTATIONS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The report said that by contrast with the Fed, the European  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governing council was not expected to begin  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 raising rates in the near term, as economic data continued to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suggest a "steady, but sluggish" recovery in Europe.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury note's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yield rose in early April above that of the German 10-year bund  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yield for the first time since October 2003,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reflecting the divergence in expected growth prospects between  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the two economies, the report noted.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the end of the quarter, the value of euro and yen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reserve holdings totaled about $19.4 billion for both the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve's System Open Market Account and the Treasury's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exchange Stabilization Fund.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Details are as follows:\par     FOREIGN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HOLDINGS OF U.S. MONETARY AUTHORITIES\par     Balance on June. 30, 2004:\par     FEDERAL RESERVE SYSTEM OPEN MARKET ACCOUNT:\par     Euro    $10.812 billion\par     Yen      $8.631 billion\par     Total   $19.443 billion\par     U.S. TREASURY EXCHANGE STABILIZATION FUND:\par     Euro    $10.797 billion\par     Yen      $8.631 billion\par     Total   $19.428 billion.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040805e0850030n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
