\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Japan fight to tame yen not the failure it appears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By David McMahon  \par \uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 19 (Reuters) - On the face of it, Japan's lonely attempt to halt the rise of the yen against the dollar appears a dismal failure.  \par \par \uc2 Despite $281 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at supporting Japan's export-led recovery, the yen continues to rise and the authorities' "line in the sand" at 105 yen looks in danger of being washed away by the tide.  \par \par \uc2 But some analysts say Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, is not necessarily fighting a losing battle.  \par \par \uc2 "I think Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been very successful in keeping the yen from doing anything that might threaten the cyclical recovery. I'd say it's been a triumph," said Richard Jerram, an economist at ING.  \par \par \uc2 Japan sold around 30.5 trillion yen ($285.5 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 14 months to the end of February, a figure that is more than three times the size of New Zealand's gross domestic product.  \par \par \uc2 That may not have halted the yen's rise completely but helped to dull it and to protect a cyclical recovery in Japan's long underperforming economy, which recently showed it was growing at its fastest clip in 13 years.  \par \par \uc2 The euro has firmed 18 percent against the dollar while sterling has gained around 14 percent since the end of 2002, compared with the yen's relatively mild rise of 11 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "The yen has also fallen on a trade-weighted basis, so in that sense we can't say that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a complete failure," says Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.  \par \par \uc2 In trade-weighted terms, the yen weakened around three percent in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 "But the fact that 20 trillion yen of spending (in 2003) still couldn't stop the yen from strengthening shows just how hard it is to support a misaligned dollar yen rate," said Tanase.  \par \par \uc2 With chances fading of an imminent U.S. interest rate rise and security jitters weighing on the dollar and euro, analysts say fundamentals point to further gains in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar will likely fall below 105 yen in the coming months, which would likely trigger a wave of stop-loss orders and drive it very quickly down to 100 yen, traders say.  \par \par \uc2 DEJA VU?  \par \par \uc2 A quick look at the numbers shows that most past efforts at \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also been failures when measured by their ability to turning around market trends.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan, acting on behalf of the Finance Ministry, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least 18 times between early 1999 and April 2000 to curb the strength of the yen, which officials worry could choke Japan's economic recovery, but the dollar continued its fall to 102 yen from around 120.  \par \par \uc2 Even one of the most successful cases of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a tough battle, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly - often in concert with Japanese and European central banks - to prop up the dollar from April 1994.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar only bottomed out after diving to a postwar low of 79.75 yen a year later.  \par \par \uc2 This time the Japanese authorities do not have the agreement of other central banks, such as the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have expressed displeasure that their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are bearing the lion's share of the burden of adjustment against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 With Japan's economy now growing at a faster pace than both the euro zone and the United States, many analysts believe it is becoming increasingly difficult for Tokyo to justify its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation intensified earlier this week after after Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki's remarks - as the dollar fell sharply with no apparent sign of support from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - that Japan would take action in the market only when needed.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki insisted on Friday that his comments were nothing out of the ordinary and said they were a "tautology".  \par \par \uc2 "The market is feeling a little confused right now," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040319e03j001an\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
