\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Markets bet against G7  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  deal.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Marie-Louise Moller  \par \uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 15:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Financial markets on Thursday bet against the weekend Group of Seven economic powers meeting agreeing on how to tackle \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings, sending the dollar lower against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 A day before the meeting starts in Florida, French Prime Minister Jean-Pierre Raffarin urged the club to agree on the need to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations distorting the world economy - a line the United States has shown little sign of backing.  \par \par \uc2 Japan also stood firm ahead of the meeting of G7 finance ministers and central bankers, saying it would act against speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves - a sign that it would not flinch at any criticism of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics.  \par \par \uc2 Despite Japan's firm position, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' eagerness to focus on growth rather than the dollar's fall at the meeting, Raffarin called for an agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Productivity...should not be undermined by inequality or great fluctuations in exchange rates which are not adapted to the reality of our economies," he said in a speech to leaders of European Union centre-right parties in Brussels.  \par \par \uc2 "We want exchange rates which are adapted to the reality of our economies. That is why I want the G7 to reach agreement on this diagnosis of the situation," Raffarin added.  \par \par \uc2 His comments failed to ease the euro's rise against the dollar, with the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  edging up to around $1.2585 - some three cents below record highs it hit in January - after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) left interest rates unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow effectively ruled out an accord on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the meeting on Friday and Saturday in Boca Raton, repeating that markets, and not governments, should set rates.  \par \par \uc2 Policymakers in Europe have stressed the risks the dollar's fall poses to euro zone exporters, but a Reuters poll of 46 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists showed few expect the G7 to say anything to stop the euro, yen, sterling and the Canadian dollar from appreciating.  \par \par \uc2 ECB CONCERNED  \par \par \uc2 ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet said after the bank left rates unchanged at 2.0 percent that it remained concerned about excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.  \par \par \uc2 "With regards to exchange rates we again particularly stress stability and express concern about exaggerated exchange rate movements," Trichet told the ECB's news conference.  \par \par \uc2 Some strategists say the summit of the G7 powers - the United States, Japan, Germany, Britain, France, Italy, and Canada - could put pressure on euro zone policy makers to cut interest rates, which are twice the 1.0 percent in the United States, increasing the attraction of holding euros.  \par \par \uc2 Allowing the yen to rise further could also spread more of the pain of dollar weakness beyond the euro zone.  \par \par \uc2 But Japan showed little sign of giving up its efforts to subdue the yen's rise. Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said the yen's recent rise posed short-term risks.  \par \par \uc2 "A strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in itself is fine for us, but in the short term we must carefully watch its impact," Fukui said. "We must watch the impact on business sentiment."  \par \par \uc2 He also said the government's repeated yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not conflict with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary easing that was aimed at lifting the country out of deflation.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese Finance Ministry took an even stronger line.  \par \par \uc2 "We will state our usual stance that sudden moves in exchange rates are undesirable and have an impact on the Japanese economy and on the world economy. And therefore, when moves are excessively speculative, we will take firm action," Vice Finance Minister Masakazu Hayashi said.  \par \par \uc2 A Canadian official said on Wednesday the G7 would discuss China, the biggest of several Asian economies whose exporters are benefitting from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  links to the weakening dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But strategists say the G7 could do little to spread the burden of the dollar's weakness beyond the group as China is not in the club.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040205e025002f9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
