\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro recovers vs majors - yen stalls on BOJ concerns.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2004\par 08:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The euro was steady against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, recovering from losses made after European officials expressed concern about excessive movement in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The yen was stuck in a narrow band on caution that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) may come under pressure to do more to increase money supply, in part to help weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on top of Japan's massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "No matter how much Japan spends on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen never stops rising, so views are growing among overseas investors that the BOJ may have to do something to boost money supply," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley Japan.  \par \par \uc2 The rise in Japan's most widely watched measure of money supply, M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs), slowed in December, up 1.5 percent from a month earlier. That compares with growth of 1.6 percent last November and 2.2 percent in December 2002.  \par \par \uc2 The sluggish growth, along with data showing a 5.1 percent drop in bank lending in December, showed that banks and borrowers were still focusing on cutting risk and debt.  \par \par \uc2 "Even if the BOJ were to pour more money into the money market, it would have a limited effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates as Japan has a structural problem of bad debts, but many foreign investors are not buying up the yen at the moment," Umemoto said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0647 GMT, the dollar was trading around 106.55 yen down slightly from 106.65 yen in late U.S. trade but within a narrow range of 106.45-72 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's downside has also been supported by recent, repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan and concerns that it could step into the market again at anytime.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Tuesday that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had been rapid given U.S. economic fundamentals and that Japan would take steps against speculative movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 TRICHET EFFECT  \par \par \uc2 The euro recovered from losses made after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) President Jean-Claude Trichet told central bankers in Basel on Monday that "excess volatility and brutal moves were not welcome and not appropriate".  \par \par \uc2 Market participants, already growing doubtful about the amount of room left for the euro to rise, started altering their positions.  \par \par \uc2 "Our stance had already been to take profits on the euro's rise as the euro is at excessively high levels," said Yuuki Sakurai, general manager at Fukoku Mutual Life Insurance's finance and investment planning department.  \par \par \uc2 The euro stood around $1.2765 recovering from the day's low of $1.2716. It hit a record high of $1.2899 in New York before Trichet's comments pulled it up.  \par \par \uc2 French Prime Minister Jean-Pierre Raffarin said officials must act quickly to bring the euro-dollar into line, but traders also pondered whether the ECB would actually move to halt a further rise in the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Last week, ECB sources said that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be futile, and there was no sense that Washington was keen to use the meeting of the Group of Seven on February 6-7 to reverse recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends.  \par \par \uc2 The market was awaiting comments from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, who is scheduled to make a speech in Berlin on globalisation at 1600 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 In particular, dealers were on the lookout for comments relating to U.S. interest rates in light of a much smaller-than-expected rise in December employment figures.  \par \par \uc2 Non-farm payrolls rose by just 1,000 last month compared with forecasts for an increase of around 145,000.  \par \par \uc2 "Whatever Greenspan says probably won't have a positive effect on the dollar. But all the same, it shouldn't be too negative," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist as JP Morgan Chase. ($1=106.64 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040113e01d001mr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
