\par\par \b \uc2 Hedge funds' role grows in  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez   \par \uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2003\par 18:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Nov 18 (Reuters) - Hedge funds, and not long-term capital flows, are increasingly driving foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, analysts say, buffeting the dollar despite fairly solid recent U.S. economic data.   \par \par \uc2 A typical hedge fund takes both long and short positions in securities or \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It uses leverage and arbitrage when possible, investing in any market where it foresees impressive gains at reduced risk.   \par \par \uc2 Included under the broad hedge fund universe are \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overlay programs set up by so-called real money accounts, such as pension, bond and equity funds. Their aim is to minimize risks by hedging the underlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their portfolio.   \par \par \uc2 Based on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends, strategists say, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are taking their cue from leveraged accounts, which rely on borrowing, and real money accounts.   \par \par \uc2 "The composition of flows in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has changed as markets have become dominated by real and leveraged accounts' investment decisions, while commercial flows (long-term foreign inflows) have become less important," said Hans Redeker, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at BNP Paribas.   \par \par \uc2 However, there is no clear, quantifiable evidence of hedge fund influence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Instead, there are only bits and pieces that when put together, seem to add up.   \par \par \uc2 "Hedge funds are definitely a major influence in this market although you cannot quantify their presence because they have different reporting requirements," said Jonathan Clark, vice chairman at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts, a money management firm in New York that oversees $1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investments.   \par \par \uc2 LIMITED IMPACT FROM LONG-TERM CAPITAL FLOWS   \par \par \uc2 BNP's Redeker said that in the third quarter, long-term capital inflows to the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  via foreign direct investment, portfolio inflows and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related flows outweighed current account outflows by around $80 billion. Yet the dollar either fell or traded within narrow ranges.   \par \par \uc2 What this suggests is that dollar selling was mostly short-term or money market-related.   \par \par \uc2 "When there's money market-related activity, this means that there was a lot of hedging going on - overlay funds hedging their portfolios, or the leveraged accounts taking advantage of the interest rate differential," Redeker said.   \par \par \uc2 Record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Asian central banks over the last six months has resulted in large dollar flows, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  persisted with its overall generalized descent.   \par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of the year, Federal Reserve custody holdings have risen by about $150 billion, helping to underpin the U.S. fixed-income market.   \par \par \uc2 "While central banks represent a significant source of demand for U.S. debt, official portfolio flows into the U.S. do not appear to have much power in explaining changes in the exchange value of the dollar," according to a Morgan Stanley report.   \par \par \uc2 A statistical analysis of quarterly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows and corresponding changes in the Fed's broad dollar index showed no significant relationship, the report added.   \par \par \uc2 HEDGE FUNDS LURED BY CARRY TRADES   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the renewed focus on interest rate differentials and carry trades - borrowing low-interest-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fund purchases of higher-yielding units - after the Reserve Bank of Australia and the Bank of England hiked rates served as a magnet to hedge funds.   \par \par \uc2 Most hedge funds still have long carry trade positions in the euro and Australian dollar against the greenback going into the end of the year. But analysts say the dollar could get a near-term boost against these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of year-end if hedge funds reverse these positions as they square their books and take profits.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031118dzbi0035l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
