\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls against yen, despite jobs data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2003\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline, dateline; previous LONDON)   \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The dollar sagged against the yen to 2-1/2-year lows below the critical 115.0 yen mark on Thursday as traders' efforts to test Japan's resolve to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen weak overwhelmed the greenback.   \par \par \uc2  The market's focus on the dollar/yen axis was intense and left considerations of economic data releases in the shade.   \par \par \uc2  Shrugging off better-than-expected U.S. jobless claims data, investors also focused some attention on the implications of the Group of Seven industrialized nations meeting in Dubai.   \par \par \uc2  But the main driver of the market remained the yen, traders said, as investors tried to test the Bank of Japan into redefining the 'line in the sand', or level at which Japan is willing to tolerate weakness in the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  The euro was up 0.23 percent on the day at $1.1311. Against the yen, the euro fell 0.62 percent to 130.17 yen.   \par \par \uc2  Sterling gained 0.43 percent against the dollar to $1.6174, continuing to benefit from expectations of an early monetary policy tightening by the Bank of England.   \par \par \uc2  Initial weekly applications for U.S. jobless benefits fell to 399,000, below the widely watched 400,000 mark and offering the dollar a temporary, but fleeting respite.   \par \par \uc2  "More than anything else, the dollar is being affected by the G7 meeting," said David Durrant, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank Julius Baer in New York. "In terms of the jobless data, 399,000 and expectations of 410,000 were not that significant. What we should look at is the continuing claims which are still rising," he said.   \par \par \uc2  YEN DRIVING MARKET   \par \par \uc2  The yen continued to tantalize the market as investors tried to test the Bank of Japan's resolve to cap yen strength.   \par \par \uc2  Both BoJ and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials in New York, however, declined to comment when asked whether the BoJ was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The Bank of Japan acts on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell over 1 percent to 115.08 yen after falling to a 2-1/2-year low earlier below 115 yen.   \par \par \uc2  "There's been a variety of sellers. I think investors are trying to test the BoJ and make it identify a line in the sand number (for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," said Ralph DelZenero, first vice president at Bank One in Chicago.   \par \par \uc2  Markets are wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan to protect a fragile export-led recovery, after record levels of official yen sales this year, but are reluctant to be short yen amid a Tokyo equities rally that has shares at 15-month peaks.   \par \par \uc2  Investors are also wary that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rebuke Japan for its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at the G7 meeting and that if Japan stands away from the market, the yen will rally sharply.   \par \par \uc2  "Markets have really pushed back expectations of Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the G7," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez.   \par \par \uc2  "It does seem that this G7 meeting has taken on a focus of its own, probably greater than it has on previous meetings. Normally we wouldn't expect to see much from the G7," he said.   \par \par \uc2  SWISS FRANC   \par \par \uc2  The Swiss National Bank left key short-term rates unchanged as expected on Thursday, saying that its near-zero rate policy is appropriate given low inflation in the Swiss economy. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Switzerland, which is mired in a double-dip recession is unlikely to recover until next year.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell 0.21 percent against the Swiss franc to 1.3757 francs. (Additional reporting by Burton Frierson in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030918dz9i002u9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
