\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar trapped near 3-wk lows, spotlight on BoJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2003\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The dollar traded near recent three week lows on the euro on Wednesday, unable to shake off doubts about the pace of U.S. recovery, while hugging a tight range on the yen on talk of persistent Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 After weeks of optimism that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' economy was turning a corner, a poor jobs reading last Friday cast doubt over its sustainability and powered a sharp downturn in the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Since last week, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shed almost five cents on the euro, retracing a substantial part of a rally that took it from record lows on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $1.1930 in June to a four-month peak of $1.0760 earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 With little economic data released in recent days, markets continued to mull over the jobs report throughout this week.  \par \par \uc2 However, later on Wednesday, a testimony by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg before the European Parliament's Economic and Monetary Affairs Committee will grab the spotlight at 1300 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow testifies before the House Financial Services Committee at 1400 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 "We have had some relatively disappointing data last Friday and the pattern has been that good data has kept the dollar steady and weak data was a strong factor against it," said David Mann, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in London.  \par \par \uc2 By 1200 GMT the dollar was firmer from the New York close at $1.1180 per euro, after trading as close as at $1.1236 from the previous session's three-week low of $1.1240.  \par \par \uc2 In Sweden, where the country holds a referendum on Sunday on whether to join Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the crown fell to a two-week low against the strengthening euro as opinion polls showed euro opponents increased their lead over euro supporters.  \par \par \uc2 DOUBTFUL RECOVERY  \par \par \uc2 Data on Friday showed a sharp fall in U.S. non-farm payrolls in August and since then there has been no major or more forward-looking data to counter investor nerves that expectations for a U.S. recovery may have got ahead of themselves.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the market is also mulling the longer term impact of the rising budget deficit, which after U.S. President George W. Bush on Sunday asked Congress for an additional $87 billion, means it will exceed $500 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "The weak payrolls number last Friday has led ultimately to lower bond yields and shakier equity markets," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in London.  \par \par \uc2 "There seems as well to be a lot of momentum driven speculative buying of euro/dollar. It's partly sparked by fundamental issues but there are also technical factors as well."  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN HOLDS DOLLAR AT BAY  \par \par \uc2 Despite the economic doubts, the dollar found support against the yen with traders in Tokyo and London suspicious of Bank of Japan dollar buying interest around 116.80-70 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Throughout Wednesday's session the greenback was trapped between 116.67-99 yen after falling to 116.10 in the previous session. The persistent upward pressure on the yen, which has driven much of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort, was also boosted on Wednesday after data showed Japan growing at its fastest pace in two and a half years in the second quarter at one percent.  \par \par \uc2 The number was revised from the preliminary 0.6 percent reading.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said this may have driven the BoJ, which acts on behalf of the finance ministry in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, to step into the market again to protect export competitiveness from the painful effect of a strong yen.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030910dz9a002et\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (United States near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs